Baseline provenance and licensing
=================================

ADAPT
  Lee et al., "Effective White-Box Testing of Deep Neural Networks with
  Adaptive Neuron-Selection Strategy", ISSTA 2020.
  Reference implementation: https://github.com/kupl/adapt
  License: MIT.
  baselines/adapt.py is a PyTorch port of that implementation and is
  distributed under the same MIT terms.

  In the reference implementation, feature f7 is indexed with an
  always-empty slice, leaving the feature dead. The port sets f7 from the
  30-40 percent weight band.

NSGen
  Huang et al., TOSEM.
  Reference implementation: https://github.com/unknownhl/NSGen
  No license is published with the reference implementation.
  baselines/nsgen.py is an independent reimplementation.

SUNTest
  Guo et al., TOSEM 2025.
  Reference implementation: https://github.com/TestingAIGroup/SUNTest
  No license is published with the reference implementation.
  baselines/suntest.py is an independent reimplementation.

The reference implementations target TensorFlow/Keras. The source files in
this repository carry no comments, so this notice records the attribution
that would otherwise appear in file headers.
